{"qid":"Q1474791","names":["Sultanate of Darfur"],"title":"Sultanate of Darfur","endonym":{"native":"سلطنة دارفور","lang":"ar"},"capsule":"The Sultanate of Darfur was an Islamic state in the western Sudan region, founded by the Keira dynasty around 1603 under Sultan Sulayman Solong, who established Islamic law and built mosques across the realm. At its height under Sultan Muhammad Tayrab (r. 1752–1785) it controlled trade routes stretching from the Sahara to the Nile corridor, extracting tribute in slaves, ivory, and ostrich feathers. The Egyptian Khedive's forces under Zubayr Rahma Mansur defeated and killed Sultan Ibrahim Qarad in 1874, annexing Darfur into the Turco-Egyptian Sudan; a brief restoration under Sultan Ali Dinar from 1898 ended when British forces killed him in battle in 1916.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Core territorial extent in the Jebel Marra highlands is well attested through Egyptian and British colonial surveys, but peripheral tributary zones fluctuated substantially and are only approximately mapped.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Darfur","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Darfur"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Sultanate of Darfur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sultanate_of_Darfur"},{"label":"R.S. O'Fahey, State and Society in Dar Fur (C. Hurst, 1980) — archive.org","url":"https://archive.org/details/stateandsocietyi0000ofah"}],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Sultanate of Darfur","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Sulayman Solong","nativeName":"سليمان صولون","roman":"Sulaymān Ṣūlūn","start":1603,"end":1637,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicens